  "limits": "Artificial register RAM and matching software shadow; native stores have ordinary RAM semantics, not device acknowledgement semantics. Supplied callback records, flags, status and direct handler invocation. Four cases first execute real configuration/start functions; eight additional cases execute configuration/start/stop-request and a separate native bit2 status reader against the same artificial RAM and shadow; no DMA completion is simulated between the native start and the directly invoked handler. Scoped code/table copies are not validated boot relocations. Stops before driver callback. Two separate real stop-request callbacks use supplied owner handles and stop before the signal trampoline; no semaphore give or caller wakeup executes. Status read-to-clear behavior is not modeled. No interrupt-controller delivery, hardware status definition, DMA, pixels, cache or frame ownership established."
